cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this analysis helps your work, cite this repository and the source datasets listed in REFERENCES.md."
type: software
title: "Ravel: Paper-driven biological research across molecular layers"
authors:
  - family-names: "Xorca"
repository-code: "https://github.com/xorca0711/ravel"
url: "https://github.com/xorca0711/ravel"
abstract: >-
  A computational research project developing testable biological questions
  through critical reading of published studies, reproduction of accessible
  findings and reanalysis of public omics and complementary experimental data.
  Papers and questions define the relevant tissues, organisms, biological units
  and methods. Source evidence, analytical results, competing explanations and
  interpretation limits are retained in a traceable research record.
keywords:
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - scanpy
  - multiomics
  - public data reanalysis
  - literature-guided research
  - hypothesis development
  - lineage tracing
date-released: 2026-09-10
